            <div xml:id="d229">

                <pb facs="0530" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg394"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">551.58B1/21</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-11-05">November 5, 1928</date>.<lb/>[Received November
                        30.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 645</seg>
                    <lb/>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">L. of N. No. 1232</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my despatch No. 619, L. of N.
                    No. 1219, of October 11, 1928, and to my telegram No. 106 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">100</hi>], of today’s date,<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d229-f1"/> I have the honor to transmit herewith a communication
                    addressed to you by the Secretary General of the League of Nations, dated
                    November 3,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d229-f2"/> inviting the American Government to
                    send duly authorized representatives to take part in an international conference
                    for the final adoption of an international convention for the suppression of
                    counterfeiting currency. The Conference is to meet at Geneva on April 9,
                    1929.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hugh R. Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
